'''Akyaung Ari''', or '''Ngachan''', is a [[Tangkhulic languages|Tangkhulic]] language spoken in Myanmar. It is most closely related to [[Somra language|Somra]].<ref name=e18/> It is spoken in Heinkut, Jagram, and Ngachan villages of [[Leshi Township]], [[Sagaing Division]], Myanmar. Ngachan shares 52% [[lexical similarity]] with [[Tangkhul language|Tanghkul Naga]] of Somra, 23% with Tangkhul Naga of Ukhrul in India, and 23% with [[Koki language|Koki Naga]].<ref name=":02">{{Cite web |date=2016 |title=Myanmar |url=http://www.ethnologue.com/country/MM/languages |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20161010180533/http://www.ethnologue.com/country/MM/languages |archive-date=2016-10-10 |website=Ethnologue: Languages of the World}}</ref>

